{
  "statement": "I assert that my sustainability requirements (GRN-01 to GRN-07) are vital for minimizing the environmental impact of the autonomous driving system. Reducing energy consumption (GRN-01) and utilizing renewable energy sources (GRN-02) are essential for achieving a lower carbon footprint. Implementing lifecycle assessments (GRN-03) ensures that the system components are environmentally friendly. Achieving high energy recovery efficiency (GRN-04) and monitoring carbon emissions (GRN-05) further enhance sustainability. Additionally, energy-efficient routing algorithms (GRN-06) and emergency protocols to minimize energy use (GRN-07) are crucial during critical failures. I see potential conflicts with EfficiencyAgent's requirements where the focus on immediate performance may compromise energy efficiency and sustainability goals.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-01", "EFF-07"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "Prioritizing speed and smoothness during maneuvers may lead to higher energy consumption and impact sustainability."
    }
  ],
  "positions": [
    {
      "id": "EFF-01",
      "stance": "oppose",
      "proposal": "Modify to integrate energy efficiency metrics alongside travel time reduction."
    },
    {
      "id": "EFF-07",
      "stance": "oppose",
      "proposal": "Change to allow relaxation of smoothness constraints in favor of energy-efficient maneuvers."
    }
  ],
